=========================================================================================================
17_dnn_nested_cv.py — Original deep network on the shared outer folds (split: random, TensorFlow environment)
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The original study scored its network once, on one random 15% test set. Here the same network,
  with the same         descriptors, preprocessing and training settings, is scored on the 25
  outer folds used for every other model of this         study, so that its accuracy can be
  compared with theirs fold by fold. Two versions are run: the baseline network on         all
  descriptors, and the complete original pipeline (descriptor selection by importance plus noisy
  copies of the         training molecules). In both, nothing about a test fold is used before
  that fold is scored.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
